16.30. Logarithms of Theta Functions of Sum and Difference
16.30.1  \frac{\ln\frac{\vartheta_{1}(\alpha+\beta)}{\vartheta_{1}(\alpha-\beta)}=\ln\frac{\sin(\alpha+\beta)}{\sin(\alpha-\beta)}}+4\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{n}\frac{q^{2n}}{1-q^{2n}}\sin2n\alpha\sin2n\beta
16.30.2  \frac{\vartheta_{2}(\alpha+\beta)}{\vartheta_{2}(\alpha-\beta)}=\ln\frac{\cos(\alpha+\beta)}{\cos(\alpha-\beta)}+4\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n}\frac{q^{2n}}{1-q^{2n}}\sin2n\alpha\sin2n\beta
16.30.3  \ln\frac{\vartheta_{3}(\alpha+\beta)}{\vartheta_{3}(\alpha-\beta)}=4\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^{n}}{n}\frac{q^{n}}{1-q^{2n}}\sin2n\alpha\sin2n\beta
16.30.4  \ln\frac{\vartheta_{3}(\alpha+\beta)}{\vartheta_{4}(\alpha-\beta)}-4\sum\limits_{n=1}^{\infty}\frac{1}{n}\frac{q^{n}}{1-q^{2n}}\sin2n\alpha\sin2n\beta
The corresponding expressions when \beta=i\gamma are easily deduced by use of the formulae 4.3.55 and 4.3.56.
